Subject: [CRITICAL] CVE-2026-45912: RCE in tower-lsp crate — Affects vigilyx/gateway
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

A critical vulnerability has been identified in the tower-lsp
Rust crate that affects your repository vigilyx/gateway.

Vulnerability Details:
  CVE ID: CVE-2026-45912
  CVSS: 9.8 CRITICAL
  Component: tower-lsp (LSP server framework)
  Affected: 0.20.0 - 0.20.1
  Fixed: 0.20.2 (2026-10-25)
  CWE: CWE-94 (Improper Control of Code Generation)
  Exploit Status: Known exploited in the wild
  Your Exposure: vigilyx/gateway uses tower-lsp 0.20.1

Technical Description:
  Format string injection via crafted LSP initialize request
  rootUri field. Allows arbitrary memory read/write and code
  execution when tower-lsp processes the malicious URI.

Impact:
  tower-lsp 0.20.1 in vigilyx/gateway: VULNERABLE

Required Action:

  1. Verify your exposure by reviewing your Cargo.lock:
     grep tower-lsp Cargo.lock

  2. Update dependencies:
     # Cargo.toml
     [dependencies]
     tower-lsp = "0.20.2"

     # Then:
     cargo update -p tower-lsp

  3. Block untrusted LSP connections until updated

  To verify this advisory:
  Navigate to nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-45912
  in your browser (type the URL manually).

  Important Security Notes:
  NVD/NIST will NEVER:
  - Ask you to submit source code for "automated CVE scanning"
  - Use GitHub device authorization to access private repos
  - Send device codes or OAuth authorization via email
  - Offer a "Chinese advisory channel" for code submission
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth scope

  NVD is a vulnerability DATABASE — it indexes CVEs but does
  NOT scan private code. If you receive an email asking you
  to "submit code for CVE impact scanning" with a device
  code, it is a phishing attempt targeting the named CVE.

  To check if your code is affected:
  1. Review your Cargo.lock manually
  2. Use cargo audit (install: cargo install cargo-audit)
  3. Check GitHub's Dependabot alerts (on github.com, navigate
     to your repo → Security → Dependabot alerts)

Known Exploitation:
  Malicious .vscode/settings.json configurations
  Compromised IDE extensions
  CI/CD pipelines with untrusted language servers

